ns not their gods — Mishnah Avodah Zarah 3:5); THE DEMOLITION SAID IN NEW WORDS — 12:3 shares two tokens in order with 7:5 and three with Exodus 34:13, 12:2 none with 7:5; FIVE VERBS where 7:5 had four, the fifth 'destroy their name' the renaming for the worse (61:7 — R. Eliezer against R. Akiva, the dispute read at chapter 7 and reread whole); 'tear down' the root's five Torah seats (7:5, 12:3, Exodus 34:13; Leviticus 11:35, 14:45 the vessel and the house); the three Asherim and the three houses the shelf's decision tables (61:5-6 — Mishnah Avodah Zarah 3:7), 'from that place' the Land as the duty's scope (61:6); 145:3's a fortiori from 12:3's burning to 16:21's planting; 'you shall not do so to the LORD your God' plural at 12:4 and singular at 12:31 — the pair's two seats (61:8's three readings; 81:5 the wrong altar). THE REGISTER: the plural half opens here — plural only at 12:2-4, both at 12:1 (the singular inside the plural verse), five of the chapter's six paragogic nuns in these four verses (1, 2, 3, 3, 4); Moses' voice, no divine frame, no narrative verb in the chapter. Onkelos: 'their errors' for their gods (the book's thirty-two rows; 12:2, 3, 30, 31), 'before the LORD' for 'to the LORD' at 12:4 — the Aramaic's reverence (the chapter's eight 'before the LORD' rows).
