VERIFIED    DV12-06 [Onkelos Deut 12:29; Onkelos Deut 12:30; Onkelos Deut 12:31; Sifrei Devarim 80:1; Sifrei Devarim 80:2; Sifrei Devarim 80:3; Sifrei Devarim 80:4; Sifrei Devarim 80:5; Sifrei Devarim 81:1; Sifrei Devarim 81:2; Sifrei Devarim 81:3; Sifrei Devarim 81:4; Sifrei Devarim 81:5; Sifrei Devarim 81:6; Sifrei Devarim 179:2] THE NATIONS CUT OFF AND THE ABOMINATION: WHEN THE LORD YOUR GOD CUTS OFF THE NATIONS WHITHER YOU GO TO DISPOSSESS THEM, AND YOU DISPOSSESS THEM AND DWELL IN THEIR LAND — TAKE HEED TO YOURSELF LEST YOU BE ENSNARED AFTER THEM AFTER THEY ARE DESTROYED FROM BEFORE YOU, AND LEST YOU INQUIRE AFTER THEIR GODS, SAYING: HOW DID THESE NATIONS SERVE THEIR GODS? AND I WILL DO SO TOO; YOU SHALL NOT DO SO TO THE LORD YOUR GOD, FOR EVERY ABOMINATION OF THE LORD WHICH HE HATES THEY DID FOR THEIR GODS — EVEN THEIR SONS AND THEIR DAUGHTERS THEY BURN IN THE FIRE TO THEIR GODS. 'When the LORD your God cuts off the nations' 12:29 and 19:1 (eight tokens; 7:1 eight), 'whither you go to dispossess them' one seat, 'and you dispossess them and dwell in their land' one — wherever you wish to build, build (80:3; 179:2 from 19:1's side, the English's '(Dt.13:29)' a wrong chapter and the Hebrew's citation right, asserted); the sages weeping at the border (80:4-5, reread whole from chapter 11); 'LEST YOU BE ENSNARED AFTER THEM' one seat — the root five in the Bible and the niphal 12:30 the one, 7:25's 'lest you be snared' ANOTHER ROOT, the Torah's one niphal of each; 'after they are destroyed from before you' one seat; 'lest you inquire after their gods' one — 12:5's verb of seeking; 'how' six in the Torah (1:12, 7:17, 12:30, 18:21, 32:30; Genesis 3:9); 'and I will do so, I too' one seat — the chapter's one 'saying', the seeker's voice, no divine frame anywhere in the chapter; the third 'take heed' a prohibition (81:1); THE ABOMINATION'S SCOPE — 'so' for the service and for the thing served (81:5 — the wrong altar's liability keyed to the Temple's rite; 12:31 the singular pair of 12:4's plural), the parents included from 'even' (81:6 — R. Akiva's witness); 'every abomination of the LORD which He hates' one seat, 'which He hates' 12:31 and 16:22 alone, 'abomination of the LORD' eight in the book (7:25; 12:31; 17:1; 18:12; 22:5; 23:19; 25:16; 27:15) and eleven in Proverbs, 'abomination' seventeen in the book; THE CHILDREN BURNED — Jeremiah 7:31's six shared tokens, 2 Kings 17:31's four, Leviticus 18:21's three; THE KING-WORD'S HOMOGRAPH — Molech's consonants are 'to the king' (the census's slip at 7:8 and 11:3), 12:31 NAMES NO MOLECH (Leviticus 18:21 and 20:2-5 the kin, credited by name); THE DB'S 13:1 IS THE ENGLISH'S 12:32 ('you shall not add nor take away' — chapter 13's reading; the chapter thirty-one verses in the Hebrew numbering, computed from the verse table). Onkelos: 'destroys the nations' for cuts off at 12:29, 'their errors' for their gods at 12:30 and 12:31, 'before the LORD' for 'to the LORD' at 12:31.
